     "result_text_tail": "med to FY2028.\n- **Stores:** all nine weak stores close in the base case; three need a board vote. With only the six whose leases end, the margin lands at about 2.98%, just under target.\n- **Basket:** the same $96 for delivery and pickup orders, since the pack gives only one average.\n\n**Numbers:** 251 in total, none missing. 99 come straight from the pack with verbatim quotes, 150 are calculations that rebuild as live formulas in the workbook, and 2 are my planning choices from the list above. The workbook grades 200 as B and 51 as E (team estimates, with their workings shown on the slide). None reach A, because the pack is the only source, so nothing could be re-checked against a second one. Of the nine hypotheses tested, 5 were confirmed, 2 revised and 2 refuted (e-commerce is profitable; deeper promotions are needed against ValuMart).\n\n**Gaps:**\n- Vendor funding fell from 55% to 46% of markdowns, but it isn't sized, because the pack has no markdown dollars. It counts as upside.\n- Two e-commerce charts would have dropped below zero, which these charts draw wrongly, so I redesigned them.\n- A few per-order dollar figures show one decimal, e.g. \"$6.4\" rather than \"$6.40\".\n\nNext, I could change the planning choices above (for example a different labor cut or promotions target) and re-render, or switch the theme.\n\nFiles are in `./deliverable/`:\n- harlow-margin-plan.pptx\n- harlow-margin-plan-sources.xlsx\n- harlow-margin-plan.json (the spec; re-render with `render.py` after edits)"
